            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Persian for to walk, then the Persian for to get on."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: دم کردن",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "دم کردن — dam kardan — \"to brew (tea); to steam (rice)\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "dam kardan pairs dam, \"breath, steam\", a native word, with kardan: to let it steam. (EtymDB also lists Arabic dam, \"blood\", a different word that looks alike.) kardan, \"to do\", is an inherited verb, from Middle Persian kardan (EtymDB)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
